{
 "_note": "MMD morph name -> DIVA face target.  This file is data, not code: it is the only place the correspondence lives, and the add-on reads it at export time.",
 "_format": "{\"mouth\": {name: DIVA mouth name}, \"expression\": {...}, \"mouth_approx\": {...}, \"expression_approx\": {...}, \"junk\": [[regex, reason], ...]}.  Keys beginning with _ are documentation and are ignored.  Values are DIVA morph names; the exporter resolves them to the numeric shape/slot through expression_slots.json and refuses any target that is not in diva_face_targets.json (i.e. not present in a SEGA shipping script).",
 "_matching_order": [
  "exact DIVA name (after normalisation)",
  "alias table (this file)",
  "the user's own worklist answers (win over everything here)",
  "keyword tier from diva_face_targets.json",
  "legal DIVA fallback",
  "report as unresolved"
 ],
 "_normalise": "NFKC, casefold, middle dot -> long mark, strip combining marks, collapse whitespace; '_', '-', '.', '/', ' ' and '　' are dropped before lookup, so mouth_open, Mouth-Open and mouth open are one key.",
